* 12au7.lib - Koren triode model for the 12AU7 / ECC82 (one triode).
*
* Norman Koren's triode equation (public, widely republished). Parameters
* below are the commonly used 12AU7 set. This is a REFERENCE device model for
* validating the Duke DI DSP against the analog stage; it is not a Zoom/Noble
* asset. Verify against a tube you measure if you need tighter fidelity.
*
* Terminals: Plate (P) Grid (G) Cathode (K)
*
*   Ep  = plate-cathode voltage       Eg = grid-cathode voltage
*   E1  = Koren intermediate          Ip = plate current
*
* Usage:  X1 plate grid cathode 12AU7
.subckt 12AU7 P G K
+ params: MU=21.5 EX=1.3 KG1=1180 KP=84 KVB=300 RGI=2000 CCG=1.6p CPG=1.5p CCP=0.4p
* grid current path (keeps bias solver honest when the grid goes positive)
RGI G Gi {RGI}
* Koren plate current
E1 E1n 0 value={ (V(P,K)/KP) * LOG(1 + EXP(KP*(1/MU + V(Gi,K)/SQRT(KVB + V(P,K)*V(P,K))))) }
* The classic Koren form writes the half-wave plate current as
* (PWR(E1,EX)+PWRS(E1,EX))/(2*KG1); PWR/PWRS are PSPICE/LTspice builtins
* ngspice does not enable by default. That expression equals pow(E1,EX)/KG1
* for E1>0 and 0 otherwise (a half-wave), so we write it with uramp()+pow(),
* which ngspice and LTspice both evaluate identically.
Gp P K value={ pow(uramp(V(E1n)), EX) / KG1 }
* interelectrode capacitances
Ccg Gi K {CCG}
Cpg Gi P {CPG}
Ccp P K {CCP}
.ends 12AU7
